            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each landmark number is 10 times the previous one. Since 1 is the first landmark number, they are all powers of 10. The following are the symbols given to these numbers —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.148,
            0.839,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.148,
                0.839,
                0.22
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>1</td><td>102 10</td><td>103 10⁵ 104</td><td>10⁶</td><td>107</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.228,
            0.848,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As in the case of Roman numbers, a given number is counted in groups of the landmark numbers, starting from the largest landmark number less than the given number. This is then used to assign the numeral."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.283,
            0.848,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example 324 which equals 100 + 100 + 100 + 10 + 10 + 4 is written as ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.331,
            0.293,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.356,
            0.847,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Represent the following numbers in the Egyptian system: 10458, 1023, 2660, 784, 1111, 70707."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.405,
            0.624,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What numbers do these numerals stand for?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.446,
            0.254,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
